The CUDA-only per-token activation quantizer is extracted from vLLM's
int8_utils.py. That file credits SGLang commit
4cb53ecd0cffceb6dee5c011a58f65997a86f151, and the kernel credits lmdeploy commit
086481ed84b59bee3b8e4274e5fc69620040c048. Their retained source URLs and immutable
vLLM extraction hashes are recorded in source-manifest.json.

Signed-int16 group-scale reads are backported from vLLM PR #48926, original
fix commit 64452fce103854b173c0d5d6c3a7ba5b7d966301, authored by lazypool and
co-authored by noonghunna. Reviewed PR head:
179d11258266ae2093dc42be925fe597d1c5103e. Only the four dense-kernel scale
reads are backported; the MoE kernel and framework are not included.

Local modifications (not claimed as upstream fixes):
- Compile only INT8 / uint4b8 / group128 / FP16-or-BF16-output kernels for SM86.
- Add standalone build/registration, typed helpers, strict metadata admission.
- Limit repack instantiations to the supported INT4/A8/no-permutation layout.
- Correct the A8 accumulator initialization bound from four N fragments to two.
- Widen signed scale multiplication and weighted accumulation to int64, with
  explicit final round-to-nearest int64-to-FP32 conversion. This prevents INT32
  wrap without inventing a carry encoding or changing quantizer rounding.
- Declare native output/workspace mutation and aliasing truthfully.

No CUDA build, numerical, sanitizer, graph, performance, or model-quality
qualification is implied. This is an explicitly experimental candidate.
Machine-readable source identities, modifications, numerical bounds, dependency
requirements, API constraints, and qualification status: source-manifest.json.
